Z||000009||jimig||02-05-2001||01:14 PM||||Here is something that happened to me about 5 years ago that may help you with your distributer problem.<BR>I had my Fiero in storage by father-in-law's garage over winter.  A pool of water formed at the low end of the garage, right where my car sat.  In spring when I took the car out, I got about 5 miles from his house when the engine died.  No warning signs or sounds.  When I started checking things over, I discovered that there was no spark coming out of the ditributer.  So I pulled it out and found a coil that is on the shaft was completely corroded.  I was unsucessful in attempting to remove this coil without damaging anything.  So then I had to find a new distributer.  Not an easy task to find one for a '85 GT.  I finally found a rebuilt one for $150.  Put it in and have not had any problems with it.<BR>Just thought it was someting worth checking. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>jimig<BR>1985 Fiero GT<BR>1968 Firebird 400 convertible<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||beer_stud_21||02-05-2001||01:14 PM||||I took the rear wheels off yesterday and had a look at the brakes.  The rear calipers are stuck "on" but I did a search of the forum and I think I can fix that.  I also have to have the rotors resurfaced.  The air cleaner box was completely rusted to hell so I tore al of it out and will be makig a ghetto ram air assembly soon.  The other thing is I think I have a dist problem, but the computer isnt giving me any codes.   hmfff...  will keep you guys updated.  Any tips you have for me are appreciated.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
